          {
            "id": "part-3-group-3",
            "type": "mcq",
            "selectCount": 1,
            "rubricHtml": "<h3>Questions 25–30</h3><p>Choose the correct letter, <strong>A</strong>, <strong>B</strong> or <strong>C</strong>.</p>",
            "questions": [
              {
                "number": 25,
                "textHtml": "Adam suggests that restaurants could reduce obesity if their menus",
                "options": [
                  {
                    "letter": "A",
                    "textHtml": "offered fewer options."
                  },
                  {
                    "letter": "B",
                    "textHtml": "had more low-calorie foods."
                  },
                  {
                    "letter": "C",
                    "textHtml": "were organised in a particular way."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "number": 26,
                "textHtml": "The students agree that food manufacturers deliberately",
                "options": [
                  {
                    "letter": "A",
                    "textHtml": "make calorie counts hard to understand."
                  },
                  {
                    "letter": "B",
                    "textHtml": "fail to provide accurate calorie counts."
                  },
                  {
                    "letter": "C",
                    "textHtml": "use ineffective methods to reduce calories."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "number": 27,
                "textHtml": "What does Rosie say about levels of exercise in England?",
                "options": [
                  {
                    "letter": "A",
                    "textHtml": "The amount recommended is much too low."
                  },
                  {
                    "letter": "B",
                    "textHtml": "Most people overestimate how much they do."
                  },
                  {
                    "letter": "C",
                    "textHtml": "Women now exercise more than they used to."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "number": 28,
                "textHtml": "Adam refers to the location and width of stairs in a train station to illustrate",
                "options": [
                  {
                    "letter": "A",
                    "textHtml": "practical changes that can influence people's behaviour."
                  },
                  {
                    "letter": "B",
                    "textHtml": "methods of helping people who have mobility problems."
                  },
                  {
                    "letter": "C",
                    "textHtml": "ways of preventing accidents by controlling crowd movement."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "number": 29,
                "textHtml": "What do the students agree about including reference to exercise in their presentation?",
                "options": [
                  {
                    "letter": "A",
                    "textHtml": "They should probably leave it out."
                  },
                  {
                    "letter": "B",
                    "textHtml": "They need to do more research on it."
                  },
                  {
                    "letter": "C",
                    "textHtml": "They should discuss this with their tutor."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "number": 30,
                "textHtml": "What are the students going to do next for their presentation?",
                "options": [
